ia & Pain Management\nCardiology\nCritical Care\nDentistry & Oral Surgery\nEmergency Medicine\nInternal Medicine\nMedical Oncology\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nOphthalmology\nRadiology\nSocial Work\nSurgery\nUrgent Care\nPrevious Slide\nNext Slide\nBoise’s 24/7 Animal Emergency Hospital and Specialty Center\nRecognized as one of the most progressive veterinary hospitals in the Northwest, WestVet Boise is part of MedVet’s nationwide network of veterinarian owned and led hospitals, offering the most advanced emergency and specialty veterinary care in the region.\nOur team of experts, many of whom are board-certified specialists, works tirelessly to provide exceptional and compassionate care to thousands of pets each year. We treat every pet as if they were our own because we know they’re an important part of your family. And our caregivers partner with your family veterinarian to ensure a complete circle of care for your pet.\nWe know pets are family! While our healthcare teams provide medical care for each pet who walks through our hospital doors, our\nVeterinary Social Work\nteam supports the people and families who love them.\nFacing an emergency? Bring your dog or cat directly to WestVet Boise – no appointment is ever needed for emergency veterinary care. Our trusted WestVet team is available 24 hours a day, 365 days a year.\nWestVet Boise Caregivers\nSearch by Name\nFilter by Specialty\nAll Specialties\nAnesthesia & Pain Management\nCardiology\nCritical Care\nDentistry & Oral Surgery\nEmergency Medicine\nInternal Medicine\nMedical Oncology\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nOphthalmology\nRadiology\nSocial Work\nSurgery\nUrgent Care\nOur Hospital Leaders\nDaniel Hume, DVM, DACVIM, DACVECC\nMedical Director\nLauren St. Claire, CVT\nHospital Director\nOur Doctors\nMaria Alcala-Galaviz\n, DVM\nCurtis  Brandt\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nMaggie  Buller\n, DVM, DACVIM (SAIM)\nInternal Medicine\nKaty  Campbell West\n, DVM, DACVS (Small Animal)\nSurgery\nKelsey Chereskin\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nLillian Corwin\n, DVM\nLorna Culver\n, VMD\nEmergency Medicine\nNell Dalton\n, DVM, MS\nUrgent Care, Emergency Medicine\nSarah Donnelly\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nAnna Elder\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nGiulia M. Ferrari\n, DVM\nAndrew Gendler\n, DVM, DACVR\nRadiology\nPaige Gilmore\n, DVM\nJustine Griesenauer\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nAlexis Grieser\n, DVM\nCarrie Hume\n, VMD, DACVIM (Oncology)\nMedical Oncology\nDaniel Hume\n, DVM, DACVIM, DACVECC\nCritical Care, Emergency Medicine, Internal Medicine\nDanielle L. Keerbs\n, DVM\nSheryl  Kepping\n, VMD\nEmergency Medicine\nAngela Kim\n, DVM\nKatherine (Casey) Leonard\n, DVM, DACVS-SA\nSurgery\nCarmen Leslie\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nNikki Licht\n, DVM, DACVECC\nEmergency Medicine, Critical Care\nKara  Lindberg\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nJustin Loudermilk\n, DVM\nSurgery\nKevin Molina\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nMikaela Montoya\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nAllison Mooney\n, DVM, DACVIM (Neurology)\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nSean Murphy\n, DVM, DACVS (Small Animal)\nSurgery\nAdam Nylund\n, DVM, MS, DACVS (Small Animal)\nSurgery\nMorgan Oakleaf\n, DVM, MS, cVMA, DACVAA\nAnesthesia & Pain Management\nVictoria Ochoa\n, DVM, MS, DACVIM\nInternal Medicine\nGrace Pechman\n, DVM\nSurgery\nSami  Pederson\n, DVM, MS, DACVO\n®\nOphthalmology\nJessica Perrucci\n, DVM, DACVECC\nCritical Care\nAlex Radtke\n, DVM, DACVR\nRadiology\nChristopher Roth\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine, Urgent Care\nGrace Scrafford\n, DVM\nAnna Sirochman\n, DVM, DACVIM (Cardiology)\nCardiology\nAbigail C. Stewart\n, DVM\nShelby Straight\n, DVM, cVMA\nEmergency Medicine\nKristin  Walker\n, DVM, DAVDC®\nDentistry & Oral Surgery\nKristine  Walters\n, DVM, DACVIM (Oncology)\nMedical Oncology\nMarjorie Wilson\n, LMSW, MPH\nSocial Work\nTaylor Yaworski\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nShow All Doctors (\n45\n)\nPet Stories\n“\nOn Sunday afternoon, I realized my cat hadn’t urinated for almost 24 hours. After an abysmal experience elsewhere, I brought her to WestVet. The difference in quality was night and day. The team’s compassion was absolutely breathtaking during this stressful day. There’s also a separate cat waiting room, which I appreciated.”\nPrevious Story\nNext Story\nFinancing Options\nWe understand that planning for the cost of care is important. Special financing and payment arrangements are available for qualified pet owners through an independent company, CareCredit.\nLearn More\nFind a location\nEmergency Care\nFind Care\nFind a Location\nFind A Doctor\nResources\nPet Care Resources\nClinical Studies\nAbout\nWe Are MedVet\nMedVet Experience\nOur Leaders\nOur Founders\nNewsroom\nDiversity, Inclusion, & Belonging\nCommunity Support\nFAQs\nContact Us\nFor Veterinarians\nClinical Studies\nContinuing Education\nCareers\nMedVet Open Positions at New Hospitals\nMedVet Training Programs\nSpecialties\nSpecialties Overview\nAnesthesia & Pain Management\nAvian & Exotics\nCardiology\nCritical Care\nDentistry & Oral Surgery\nDermatology\nEmergency Medicine\nIntegrative Medicine\nInternal Medicine\nInterventional Radiology\nMedical Oncology\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nOphthalmology\nRadiation Oncology\nRadiology\nRehabilitation\nSports Medicine\nSurgery\nUrgent Care\nSocial\nInstagram\nLinkedIn\nFacebook\nYouTube\nPartners\nVetRad\nVeterinary Eye Institute\nMedVet Suppliers\nLegal\nPrivacy Policy\nCA Privacy\nYour Privacy Choices\nTerms\nTransparency in Coverage\nTax Information",
